Updates ops/status.md (session summary) and ops/changelog.md with the
exp5600 leave-one-game-out gate result and the exp5574 artifact/code mismatch
disclosure from the prior commit (b9a228bd1). Also records an operational
incident: mid-session, the actively-running conductor reverted this
session's uncommitted working-tree changes back to HEAD via a git operation
inside one of its own unrelated tasks. No data was permanently lost
(recovered from conversation history, re-committed), but it's a new
concurrent-modification hazard the existing "Never Stash — Always
Commit-First" discipline doesn't cover.

ops/known-issues.md's task 8 update is NOT included in this commit -- it is
blocked by the overdue-priority-lint pre-commit hook (an unrelated,
pre-existing stale priority, pending_count=275, about
scripts/retro_timing_fallback.py's import wiring, whose prepared fix touches
the shared conductor script and was denied by the auto-mode classifier). The
known-issues.md edit remains staged on disk pending a decision.

